// A bare `Map()` in ARGUMENT position, against a parameter whose map VALUE is not the mono
// i32. `vl check` returns 0 and the engine refuses the module: the constructor read the
// ambient `pendingMapSlot` (-1, the mono `$mapStruct`) while the parameter's valtype is the
// value-typed map struct.
//
// Every sibling position seeds the shape before the constructor builds — the annotated
// binding (`emitLetDeclStmt`), the global cell (`emitAssign`'s global arm) and the result
// annotation (`emitReturnValue`'s `retMap`), whose own comment names the failure this is:
// "INVALID-WASM … for EVERY non-mono value type". The ARGUMENT boundary never grew it.
//
// The i32-valued spelling escapes because `{[string]: i32}` IS the mono shape, and a
// VARIABLE argument escapes because its binding already seeded the shape. See D1223.
// Should print 0 then 0 then 0.
function takeStr(m: {[string]: string}): i32 { m.size }
function takeF64(m: {[string]: f64}): i32 { m.size }
function takeI32(m: {[string]: i32}): i32 { m.size }

print(takeStr(Map()))
print(takeF64(Map()))
print(takeI32(Map()))
